<Base title="About | The Fault Code" description="How The Fault Code works: furnace, washer, dishwasher and AC / heat pump error codes taken from manufacturer manuals and official support pages, nothing guessed, with safety guidance and a link to the source on every page.">
<div class="wrap prose"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">About</li></ol></nav><div class="card" style="margin-top:12px"><h1>About</h1><p>This site lists error codes for furnaces, washing machines, dishwashers and AC / heat pumps and what they mean, taken from the manufacturers' installation and service manuals or official support pages. Each code page links to the document it came from.</p><p>We only publish codes we could check against a manufacturer manual or official support page. If we could not read or confirm a code, we left it out.</p><p>This is general information, not professional advice. Gas furnaces can be dangerous. If you smell gas, leave the building and call your gas utility. For anything beyond basic checks, call a licensed HVAC technician (or a qualified appliance technician for washers and dishwashers).</p><p>Browse <a href="/codes/">all codes</a> or read the <a href="/guides/">guides</a> (currently furnace-focused).</p><p>Found a mistake? Check the linked manual for your exact model; manuals vary by model and revision.</p></div></div>
</Base>
